# LuxeMarket — Backend

FastAPI backend with PostgreSQL, Redis caching, and a scikit-learn valuation model.

## Requirements

- Python 3.12+
- Docker Desktop

## Quickstart

```bash
make up          # start Postgres + Redis
make migrate     # run DB migrations
make seed        # seed 1,500 listings
make valuate     # compute valuations + deal scores
make dev         # start API server at localhost:8000
make test        # run test suite (50+ tests)
```

## Environment variables

Copy `.env.example` to `backend/.env`.

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | `postgresql://luxe:luxe_dev@localhost:5432/luxemarket` | Postgres connection |
| `REDIS_URL` | `redis://localhost:6379` | Redis connection |
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | Environment name |
| `SECRET_KEY` | `change_me_in_production` | App secret |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Logging level |

## API endpoints

Full interactive docs at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/v1/health` | Liveness + DB + Redis status |
| GET | `/api/v1/listings` | Paginated listings with filters |
| GET | `/api/v1/listings/top-deals` | Listings with deal score ≥ 60 |
| GET | `/api/v1/listings/{id}` | Single listing with valuation |
| POST | `/api/v1/listings/search` | Full-text + faceted search |
| GET | `/api/v1/makes` | All makes with counts |
| GET | `/api/v1/makes/{make}/models` | Models for a make |
| GET | `/api/v1/trends` | Market snapshots by make/model |
| GET | `/api/v1/trends/summary` | Dashboard summary stats |
| GET | `/api/v1/valuations/{listing_id}` | Valuation detail |
| POST | `/api/v1/jobs/valuate` | Trigger valuation pipeline |
| GET | `/api/v1/jobs/valuate/status` | Job status |

## Caching

Redis caches all list and trend endpoints. TTLs:

| Endpoint | TTL |
|---|---|
| `/listings` | 60s |
| `/listings/top-deals` | 120s |
| `/trends` | 300s |
| `/trends/summary` | 120s |
| `/makes` | 300s |
| `/listings/search` | 45s |

## Valuation model

Ridge regression trained on make, model, year, mileage, condition, body style,
and location. Log-transform applied to price and mileage before training.

- Cross-val R²: **0.947 ± 0.002**
- Deal score: `((estimated_value - price) / estimated_value * 100 + 20) / 40 * 100`, clipped 0–100

## Tests

```bash
pytest tests/ -v   # 50+ tests across all endpoint groups
```